  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 454.39pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 477.55pt, "Deep-ultraviolet (DUV) microscopy can provide label-free biochemical contrast by exploiting the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 490.15pt, "intrinsic absorption of nucleic acids, proteins and lipids, offering chemically specific morphological ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.75pt, "information that complements structural optical thickness contrast from phase-sensitive imaging. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 515.47pt, "However, existing DUV microscopes typically rely on specialized optics and DUV-sensitive cameras, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 528.07pt, "which restrict field of view, increase system complexity and cost, and often require high illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 540.79pt, "doses that risk photodamage. Here, we report a low-dose deep-UV lensless holographic microscopy ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.42pt, "platform that uses standard board-level CMOS sensors designed for visible light, eliminating all imaging ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 566.02pt, "optics and dedicated DUV detectors. Our system achieves large field-of-view (up to 116 mm²) DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.74pt, "imaging with low illumination and label-free phase and chemically specific amplitude contrast. A ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 591.34pt, "specialized defocus/wavelength diverse pixel super-resolution reconstruction with total-variation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 604.06pt, "regularization and robust autofocusing halves the effective sensor pixel pitch and yields down to 870 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.66pt, "nm lateral resolution. We demonstrate chemically specific, label-free bioimaging on challenging ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 629.26pt, "specimens, including ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165.86pt, 629.26pt, "Saccharomyces cerevisiae")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.49pt, 629.26pt, ", extracellular vesicles and unstained mouse liver tissue. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.98pt, "In liver sections, imaging at λ = 330 nm reveals lipid- and retinoid-rich accumulations that co-localize ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 654.58pt, "with Oil Red O staining, enabling label-free identification of hepatic stellate (Ito) cells. This combination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 667.3pt, "of low-dose operation, chemically specific contrast and standard CMOS hardware establishes DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.9pt, "lensless holographic microscopy as a practical and scalable route to high-content submicron-resolution ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 692.62pt, "whole-slide preparation-free bioimaging without exogenous labels. ")
]

