#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 234.5pt), 70.5pt, 444.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.02pt, "UV imaging approach, which further illustrates the growing interest in DUV-enabled label-free ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 93.74pt, "modalities")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(116.78pt, 89.78pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.74pt, 93.74pt, ". Lensless holography significantly reduces cost and system complexity")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(448.54pt, 89.78pt, "21–23")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(465.94pt, 93.74pt, ". In addition, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 106.34pt, "standard CMOS cameras originally designed for the visible range provide sufficient sensitivity in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 119.06pt, "DUV band. This eliminates the need for costly UV-optimized detectors and further reduces the overall ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 131.66pt, "system cost without compromising imaging performance. Because the sample is placed in close ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 144.26pt, "proximity to the sensor (around 1-2 mm), the effective FOV is determined only by the sensor area. Such ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 156.98pt, "a large FOV is particularly beneficial for high-throughput applications such as digital pathology, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 169.58pt, "cytology, and large-area cell/tissue screening")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(276.89pt, 165.62pt, "24,25")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.63pt, 169.58pt, ". Importantly, LH has also demonstrated excellent ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 182.3pt, "performance under low photon illumination conditions, maintaining high phase reconstruction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 194.9pt, "quality")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(101.54pt, 190.94pt, "26,27")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(117.26pt, 194.9pt, ". This highlights the intrinsic efficiency of lensless architectures, which require significantly ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 207.5pt, "lower illumination intensities compared to conventional optical setups,")
  #line-at(432.58pt, 207.5pt, "thereby")
  #line-at(473.74pt, 207.5pt, "minimizing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 220.34pt, "phototoxicity.  ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 240.89pt, "In this work, we present a straightforward and cost-effective platform for Lensless Holographic Deep ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 253.49pt, "Ultraviolet (LH-DUV) microscopy. This label-free system integrates a new robust computational pixel ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 266.21pt, "super-resolution")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(142.22pt, 262.25pt, "28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.18pt, 266.21pt, " (PSR) with total-variation (TV) denoising")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(343.03pt, 262.25pt, "29")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(349.99pt, 266.21pt, " and darkfield autofocusing to achieve ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 278.81pt, "large FOV, high-contrast, molecularly sensitive imaging of biological samples under low illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 291.53pt, "and deploying regular camera. Because DUV absorption is intrinsically tied to specific molecular bonds, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 304.13pt, "LH-DUV simultaneously provides amplitude contrast with inherent biochemical specificity and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 316.73pt, "complementary quantitative phase imaging. To demonstrate the capabilities of LH-DUV bioimaging, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 329.45pt, "we validated the system on yeast cells, extracellular vesicles (EVs), and mouse liver tissue. This novel ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 342.05pt, "platform combines wide-area imaging, low photon budget operation, chemical specificity, and low cost ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 354.77pt, "(few optomechanical parts and a regular VIS camera), which makes it a promising tool for applications ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 367.49pt, "in digital pathology, cytology, and life sciences. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.59pt, "Results  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 443.59pt, "Experimental Setup and Reconstruction Strategy ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 470.47pt, "The experimental platform is based on a simple LH configuration designed to enable cost-effective, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 483.07pt, "large FOV imaging in the DUV regime (Fig. 1). The sample was positioned as close to the sensor as it ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 495.79pt, "could be (approximately 1-2 mm, depending on measured sample) to achieve ~1x magnification (with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 508.39pt, "FOV equal to the camera size), and plane-wave illumination was used. The scattered and unscattered ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 521.11pt, "components of a wavefront interfere directly on the detector, producing an in-line Gabor hologram. In ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 533.71pt, "the simplest configuration, this hologram can be numerically back-propagated to the sample plane, e.g., ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 546.43pt, "using the angular spectrum")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.61pt, 542.47pt, "30")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.57pt, 546.43pt, " (AS) method.")
  #line-at(281.45pt, 546.43pt, "However, such reconstruction would be spoiled by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 559.06pt, "reconstruction artefacts")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(173.33pt, 555.1pt, "31")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(180.29pt, 559.06pt, " due to missing phase information in camera plane and lateral resolution limited ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 571.78pt, "by the pixel size of the used camera.  ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 592.3pt, "In our study, we employed a data multiplexing strategy that enables to simultaneously minimize the twin ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 605.02pt, "image artefacts and bypass the pixel size resolution limitation with the PSR algorithm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(448.9pt, 601.06pt, "28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(455.86pt, 605.02pt, ". The employed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 617.62pt, "experimental system was capable to work with two equivalent data multiplexing modes: (i) axial multi-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 630.34pt, "distance (various sample-camera distances) and (ii) multi-wavelength (different illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 642.94pt, "wavelengths). Both approaches provide the hologram-domain sub-pixel diversity required to surpass the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 655.54pt, "native sensor pitch that limits sampling-driven resolution; data acquired with both diversity methods ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 668.26pt, "were processed using the same PSR reconstruction procedure. Importantly, the employed reconstruction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 680.86pt, "algorithm was adapted to low intensity (low signal-to-noise ratio, SNR) holograms - which can result ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 693.58pt, "due to DUV source and VIS camera spectral mismatch and minimizing exposure time to reduce ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 706.18pt, "photodamage - by additionally supporting it with TV. The proposed reconstruction procedure is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 718.8pt, "described in details in the Methods section. A representative hologram (blue frame in Fig. 1(a)) and its ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 731.64pt, "reconstruction (Fig. 1(b)) resolving fine mouse liver tissue features are shown (in amplitude) in Fig. 1. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 752.16pt, "Illumination was provided by a tunable nanosecond pulsed laser, enabling direct comparison between ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 764.76pt, "VIS and DUV reconstructions. For one validation experiment (shown in Fig. 2), a fixed-wavelength ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 454pt), 70.5pt, 154.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.02pt, "DUV laser was also employed to demonstrate that the method can operate effectively with simpler and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 93.74pt, "lower-cost light sources when employing an axial multi-distance diversity configuration. This highlights ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 106.34pt, "that while spectral tunability facilitates systematic wavelength-dependent analysis, the core lensless ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 119.18pt, "configuration remains compatible with standard single-wavelength DUV illumination. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 339.53pt, "Figure 1. (a) Scheme of the LH-DUV setup. The sample is illuminated by a plane wave, and the camera is placed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.05pt, "in close proximity to the sample (~1–2 mm). Unscattered and scattered components of the transmitted field ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 362.57pt, "interfere directly on the sensor, forming an in-line Gabor hologram. Multi-frame acquisition for PSR ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 374.09pt, "reconstruction is achieved either by varying the sample–camera distance through axial camera displacement or by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 385.49pt, "tuning the illumination wavelength of the laser source. (b) Representative PSR amplitude reconstruction of a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 397.03pt, "mouse liver section hologram recorded using 340 nm wavelength, illustrating the large accessible FOV and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 408.55pt, "resolving fine DUV-specific histological features. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 462.79pt, "Low-photon budget operation in DUV with VIS-specified cameras ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 489.67pt, "To validate that CMOS cameras originally designed for the visible range can also operate in the LH-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.27pt, "DUV, and to highlight the inherent capability of LH-DUV to maintain resolution even under extremely ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 514.99pt, "low illumination")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.7pt, 511.03pt, "26,27")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(161.3pt, 514.99pt, ", we conducted a series of experiments with controlled exposure times using a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.59pt, "board-level VIS camera with 1.45 µm pixel size. In the DUV case, the optical power reaching the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 540.31pt, "detector (camera plane) was below the sensitivity of any of our available power meters (<100 µW), ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 552.94pt, "underlining the low-light conditions of the experiment. Because no direct measurement of such weak ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 565.54pt, "power levels was possible, we required an alternative way to control and quantify the effective ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.26pt, "illumination. To this end, we kept the illumination constant and systematically reduced the camera ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 590.86pt, "exposure time. In this manner, we were able to indirectly emulate progressively lower doses of incident ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 603.58pt, "light, while ensuring that the level of signal recorded by the sensor was well controlled. This approach ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.18pt, "allowed us to demonstrate that reconstructions with maintained spatial resolution can still be achieved ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 628.9pt, "from data acquired at the very limit of detectable hologram intensity. DUV measurements in this section ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.62pt, "were performed at  λ = 266 nm,")
  #line-at(213.17pt, 641.62pt, "and the data used for PSR were acquired in the multi-distance mode. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 668.14pt, "Figure 2 presents four datasets (rows) corresponding to different camera exposure times (0.3, 0.5, 1, and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 680.74pt, "15 ms), each reconstructed using three distinct algorithms. The first column shows Gabor ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 693.46pt, "reconstructions obtained via the AS method, which (contrary to PSR) was performed from only a single ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 706.06pt, "hologram. The second column presents PSR reconstruction results, and the third column displays PSR ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 718.8pt, "results further enhanced with TV and autofocusing. The last column illustrates the effective bit depth of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 731.4pt, "a single hologram for each representative exposure dataset. As shown, the application of PSR ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 744pt, "consistently improves resolution, while additional TV denoising effectively suppresses noise. A detailed ")
]

