  #line-at(70.824pt, 522.55pt, "Because yeast are phase objects, the VIS reconstructions exhibit none amplitude contrast, whereas in the DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 534.07pt, "regime the cells appear with strong contrast in both amplitude and phase. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 587.02pt, "Figure 5 presents reconstructions of EVs obtained under VIS (λ = 500 nm) and DUV (λ = 260 nm) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 599.74pt, "illumination. As in the yeast experiment, rectangular panels show the full amplitude FOV reconstruction, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 612.34pt, "while the circular insets separate the amplitude (Amp) and phase (Ph) components. EVs were prepared ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 624.94pt, "in PBS between two coverslips and exhibited rapid drying between acquisitions. To enable a fair ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 637.66pt, "comparison (same refractive index difference), PBS was replenished before the VIS measurement, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 650.26pt, "which introduced additional larger debris visible only in the VIS FOV. Despite these practical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 662.98pt, "differences, the contrast behavior remains robust: under DUV illumination, EVs exhibit strong ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 675.58pt, "amplitude contrast mainly due to RNA absorption near 260 nm and increased light scattering, while in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 688.3pt, "VIS they appear primarily as weak phase features.")
]

// arXiv source page 9
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-09.png", width: 431.5pt), 82pt, 70.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 302.21pt, "Figure 5. Comparison of PSR reconstructions of EVs under VIS and DUV illumination. The full FOVs are shown ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 313.73pt, "in amplitude, while the circular insets display both amplitude and phase. As EVs are weakly scattering phase ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 325.25pt, "objects in visible range, the VIS reconstructions provide negligible amplitude contrast and only faint phase ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 336.77pt, "signatures. In contrast, DUV illumination yields markedly enhanced visibility, with EVs in both amplitude ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 348.29pt, "(increased absorption of RNA and vesicle scattering) and phase channels. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 401.23pt, "We next imaged 30 µm thick unstained mouse liver sections using the lensless setup under both VIS ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.95pt, "and DUV illumination, Fig. 6. The large amplitude FOV of the tissue is shown at the top, with the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 426.55pt, "marked region indicating the area enlarged below. Under VIS illumination (λ = 650 nm), the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 439.27pt, "reconstructed amplitude image shows no clear subcellular features. In contrast, under DUV illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 451.87pt, "(λ = 330 nm), numerous punctate structures become clearly visible in amplitude. Based on their ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 464.47pt, "morphology and distribution, we hypothesize that these features correspond to lipid-laden hepatic ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 477.19pt, "stellate cells (HSCs). HSCs (also known as Ito cells) are localized in the space of Disse between ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 489.79pt, "hepatocytes and sinusoidal endothelium. In their quiescent state, HSCs serve as reservoirs for vitamin ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.51pt, "A stored in lipid droplets. Morphologically, they display a stellate appearance with multiple cytoplasmic ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 515.11pt, "projections, and their nuclei have smooth contours")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.83pt, 511.15pt, "32")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(300.79pt, 515.11pt, ". Strong contrast in DUV comes from the selective ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.71pt, "absorption of retinoids, which have characteristic absorption bands near 330 nm. Such absorption is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 540.43pt, "absent in the visible range, explaining why the same structures are not detectable in VIS amplitude. To ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.06pt, "validate our hypothesis, the same liver section was stained with Oil Red O (ORO) and re-imaged in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 565.78pt, "lensless system at a VIS wavelength of 632.8 nm. The resulting amplitude map reproduced the punctate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.38pt, "distribution observed in the UV reconstruction. Independent Fourier ptychographic microscopy (FPM) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 590.98pt, "measurement, performed using our custom-built system designed for high space-bandwidth product ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 603.7pt, "reconstruction")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.82pt, 599.74pt, "33,34")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.54pt, 603.7pt, ", further confirmed the co-localization of stained lipids and unstained features ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.3pt, "observed in LH-DUV (see Fig. 7). Quiescent HSCs are readily visualized using ORO histochemical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 629.02pt, "staining, where lipid (retinoid) droplets appear intensely red. ORO staining in the case of activated HSCs ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.62pt, "is very weak or not visible")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.49pt, 637.66pt, "35")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(194.33pt, 641.62pt, ". Together, these results indicate that LH-DUV imaging can reveal retinoid ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 654.22pt, "(lipid) accumulations without staining and reproduce the similar structures highlighted by ORO ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 666.94pt, "histochemistry features not detectable in VIS. This provides label-free high-throughput chemical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.54pt, "specificity in histopathological application, here preliminarily applied - for the first time - to HSCs ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 692.38pt, "activation screening. ")
]

