// arXiv source page 11
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-11.png", width: 453pt), 71pt, 70.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 403.75pt, "Figure 7. Co-localization of LH-DUV reconstructions with ORO-stained FPM images of mouse liver tissue. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 415.27pt, "large background panel shows the FOV obtained with the LH-DUV system (LL FOV), overlaid with the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 426.79pt, "corresponding high-resolution FPM FOV. Circular insets highlight representative regions demonstrating a strong ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 438.31pt, "spatial correspondence between lipid-rich structures detected by the LH-DUV modality (rendered in grayscale) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 449.71pt, "and the ORO-stained features visualized with FPM (marked in red). Across the entire overlapping FOV, lipid ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 461.23pt, "droplets exhibit consistent positional agreement in both modalities, confirming that DUV-induced contrast ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 472.75pt, "robustly identifies lipid-rich microstructures related to Ito cells without the need for chemical staining. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 524.11pt, "Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.06pt, "This work presents a first demonstration of chemical contrast in high-throughput label-free LH-DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 565.78pt, "imaging. Many biomolecules including proteins, nucleic acids, and lipids, exhibit strong and selective ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.38pt, "absorption bands in the DUV. By tuning the illumination wavelength to these specific bands, it becomes ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 591.1pt, "possible to visualize and differentiate molecular components without extrinsic staining. This was ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 603.7pt, "exemplified by the detection of retinoid-rich hepatic stellate cells in unstained mouse liver tissue, where ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.3pt, "characteristic absorption at 330 nm produced strong amplitude contrast, revealing specific retinoid-rich ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 629.02pt, "structures that were effectively invisible under visible light illumination. For EVs - imaged for the first ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.62pt, "time here in DUV and without lenses - which are enriched with nuclear acids (small non-codding RNA ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 654.34pt, "mostly) their amplitude visibility was achieved at 260 nm within absorption characteristic for RNA ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 666.94pt, "molecules")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.58pt, 662.98pt, "36–38")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.98pt, 666.94pt, ". Taking into consideration that average EV dimension is in a range between 50 and 300 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.54pt, "nm, one observes increased scattering in DUV which additionally amplifies holographic signal - a clear ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 692.26pt, "advantage of LH-DUV. The LL-DUV capabilities are particularly powerful because it eliminates the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 704.86pt, "need for conventional staining procedures, which are often time-consuming, variable, and sample ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 717.6pt, "destructive. By enabling intrinsic chemical contrast directly from the specimen, LH-DUV provides a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 730.2pt, "faster (large FOV and high-throughput), simpler, and non-invasive alternative to standard histological ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 743.04pt, "methods. ")
]

// arXiv source page 12
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.02pt, "One of the main critical aspect of this work is the demonstration of quantitative lensless holographic ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 93.74pt, "DUV imaging under low dose (illumination). Gorti et al. previously studied that under DUV imaging ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 106.34pt, "conditions (255 nm, ~1 nW/µm², 50 ms exposure) more than 20,000 sequential acquisitions can be ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 119.06pt, "performed before reaching the photodamage threshold (1 µJ/µm²)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(373.75pt, 115.1pt, "17")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.71pt, 119.06pt, ". In our experiments, the DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 131.66pt, "illumination reaching the detector was below the minimum detection limit of our power meter (PM100D ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 144.26pt, "with S175C sensor, Thorlabs), whose active area is 18 mm ×18 mm. Even if the minimum detectable ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 156.98pt, "power (100 µW) were used in this calculation, it would correspond to a surface power density of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 169.58pt, "approximately 0.00031 nW/µm² - already three orders of magnitude lower than threshold that was ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 182.3pt, "considered as safe for imaging in the mentioned work")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.71pt, 178.34pt, "17")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.55pt, 182.3pt, ". Since the signal remained below the detection ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 194.9pt, "floor, the actual delivered dose was actually much lower. This provides strong evidence that our ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 207.5pt, "illumination levels are orders of magnitude below reported cytotoxic DUV doses, supporting the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 220.34pt, "compatibility of the proposed LH-DUV imaging technique with sensitive or live specimens.  ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 246.89pt, "A central numerical contribution of this work is the implementation of PSR strategy specifically adapted ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 259.49pt, "to low illumination intensity in LH-DUV by supporting it with TV denoising and robust darkfield driven ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 272.21pt, "autofocusing")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.82pt, 268.25pt, "40")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.78pt, 272.21pt, ". The algorithm operates seamlessly in both multi-distance and multi-wavelength ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 284.81pt, "acquisition modes, offering complementary advantages. The multi-distance mode relies on a single ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 297.53pt, "fixed-wavelength laser and simple axial translations, making it particularly well suited for standard ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 310.13pt, "laboratory environments where tuneable sources may not be available. By contrast, the multi-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 322.73pt, "wavelength mode requires no mechanical motion and is ideal for studies where the imaging system must ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 335.45pt, "remain completely static, for example, when imaging live delicate biological samples. The robustness ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 348.05pt, "of the reconstruction process under both modes stems from the use of a global Fourier transform ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 360.77pt, "framework (central to the hologram propagation - numerical refocusing - procedure), which effectively ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 373.37pt, "exploits information redundancy across the full sensor area. In other words, each point in the object ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 385.97pt, "plane scatters onto the entire sensor creating a hologram, while global Fourier transform uses all pixels ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 398.71pt, "in the hologram (image) domain to calculate each pixel in the spectral domain and allow for propagation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 411.31pt, "(refocusing). These features enable the holographic reconstruction algorithm to remain stable even under ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 424.03pt, "extremely low signal conditions, as the large number of pixels is more important than detected intensity ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 436.75pt, "dynamic range in each pixel. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 463.27pt, "Despite these advantages, several limitations warrant consideration. First, the dose was indirectly ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 475.99pt, "controlled via exposure time because the incident power was below meter sensitivity; future work should ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 488.59pt, "calibrate absolute radiant exposure and photons-per-pixel to enable quantitative dose-response analysis. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 501.19pt, "Second, usable wavelengths depended on substrate transmission (standard microscope glass absorbs ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 513.91pt, "strongly at ~300 nm and entirely blocks shorter DUV wavelengths); systematic evaluation of common ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 526.51pt, "substrates and the adoption of fused silica or quartz coverslips could help extend the accessible spectral ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 539.23pt, "range, albeit at increased system cost. It should also be noted that not only the substrate material but also ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 551.86pt, "the immersion medium can strongly absorb DUV light, so it should be chosen carefully. While the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 564.46pt, "achieved lateral resolution of 870 nm in proposed LH-DUV method already provides high-quality ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 577.18pt, "submicron imaging, it does not yet reach the theoretical diffraction limit set by the illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 589.78pt, "wavelength. Because DUV illumination inherently supports higher resolution, using a detector with a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 602.5pt, "smaller pixel pitch would make it possible to overcome the current sampling bottleneck and approach ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 615.1pt, "the wavelength-limited resolution of the system. At present, the main constraint lies in the fabrication ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 627.7pt, "of sensors with insufficiently small pixels, which can be further numerically reduced in size by 2 via ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 640.54pt, "PSR. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 667.06pt, "All presented results position novel LH-DUV imaging as a powerful and practical modality for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.66pt, "quantitative, chemically specific, label-free bioimaging at extremely low illumination levels in large ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 692.38pt, "FOV deploying regular VIS CMOS sensors. Its combination of cost efficiency, optical simplicity, and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 704.98pt, "robust reconstruction makes it a promising platform for large-area tissue imaging, high-throughput bio-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 717.72pt, "chemical screening, and future live-cell studies, with potentially impactful applications in biomedicine, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 730.44pt, "biophotonics and disease diagnostics. ")
]

// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-13.png", width: 278.5pt), 70.5pt, 111pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81.98pt, "Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 109.82pt, "Setup details  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 136.7pt, "The system employed plane-wave illumination to ensure uniform magnification")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(429.7pt, 132.74pt, "39")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(436.54pt, 136.7pt, " across all recorded ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 149.3pt, "holograms. The tunable laser used in most experiments was the Ekspla NT242 (programmable range ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 162.02pt, "210-2100 nm, tuning resolution 1 nm, FWHM linewidth 3-5 cm⁻¹,")
  #line-at(365.23pt, 162.02pt, "pulse duration 3-6 ns, repetition rate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 174.62pt, "1 kHz). The wavelength selection was achieved by fine adjustments inside the optical parametric ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 187.22pt, "oscillator resonator, allowing discrete tuning steps. To validate the applicability of the approach using ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 199.94pt, "simpler light sources, a fixed-wavelength DUV laser (Teem Photonics SNU-02P-100, λ = 266 nm, pulse ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 212.54pt, "duration ≈ 550 ps, repetition rate ≈ 6 kHz, output energy > 0.3 µJ) was employed in the low-illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 225.38pt, "CMOS validation experiment described in Results section (Fig. 1). ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 251.93pt, "In the experiments, we employed two different VIS board-level CMOS cameras: Allied Vision Alvium ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 264.53pt, "1800 U-2050m Bareboard (5496 × 3672 pixels, 2.4 µm pixel size) and iDS uEye+ U3-38J2XLE Rev. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 277.13pt, "1.2 (3864 × 2176 pixels, 1.45 µm pixel size), to demonstrate the versatility of the method. Although ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 289.85pt, "both cameras are specified for the visible spectral range, they exhibited sufficient sensitivity in the DUV, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 302.45pt, "allowing the use of standard, low-cost detectors without requiring specialized DUV-optimized sensors. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 315.17pt, "This is possible because board-level CMOS sensors are used without front-end optics, so the incident ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 327.77pt, "DUV light directly reaches the photodiode layer. Apart from a thin protective cover plate, typically made ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 340.49pt, "of silicon or fused silica with good DUV transmittance, no additional optical elements are present to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 353.09pt, "attenuate the signal. This simple configuration ensures that the quantum efficiency, although reduced ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 365.69pt, "compared to VIS, remains sufficient for lensless holographic reconstruction. According to the available ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 378.41pt, "data sheets, the quantum efficiency of the Allied Vision camera is approximately 5.7% at 320 nm, while ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 391.13pt, "that of the iDS camera reaches about 37% at 400 nm. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 417.67pt, "Importantly, unlike conventional lens-based systems, the LH-DUV image reconstruction process relies ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 430.39pt, "on a global transformation of the entire raw image captured by the camera, enabling the recovery of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 442.99pt, "object information even under low DUV intensity conditions. Specifically, the key element of LH-DUV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 455.59pt, "reconstruction is the Fourier transform, which is a global operation-meaning that all pixels in the image ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 468.31pt, "domain contribute to the calculation of each pixel value in the Fourier domain, and vice versa. Likewise, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 480.91pt, "in LH-DUV, each object point is redundantly encoded by many sensor pixels, allowing robust recovery ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 493.63pt, "of object information despite low intensity levels in individual pixels. This combination of direct sensor ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 506.23pt, "illumination, absence of front-end optics, and global phase retrieval makes the configuration both cost-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 518.95pt, "efficient and technically powerful, crucially for exotic and powerful DUV regime. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 574.3pt, "Pixel-super resolution lensless holographic reconstruction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 601.18pt, "We employed a multi-frame strategy implemented in two alternative acquisition modes: (i) axial multi-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 613.78pt, "distance, in which a set of holograms are recorded at various propagation distances using a single ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 626.5pt, "illumination wavelength, and (ii) multi-wavelength, in which holograms are successively recorded in a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 639.1pt, "motion-free fashion at different illumination wavelengths. In both modes, the resulting sequence of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 651.7pt, "holograms - each with distinct fringe patterns with spatially shifted Gabor fringes - provides the sub-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 664.42pt, "pixel diversity required to surpass the native sensor pitch limitation. For reconstruction, the two modes ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 677.02pt, "are operationally equivalent: the same registration and PSR pipeline is applied, differing only in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 689.74pt, "source of diversity (z-distance versus wavelength). The use of plane-wave illumination and the short ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 702.34pt, "sample-to-sensor distance ensures identical magnification across all frames, regardless of the PSR mode ")
