  #line-at(228.65pt, 244.37pt, "11.12 ")
  #line-at(344.71pt, 244.37pt, "6.94 ")
  #line-at(458.02pt, 244.37pt, "6.13 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 283.97pt, "To further investigate the impact of signal level on reconstruction noise, we conducted an additional ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 296.69pt, "experiment in which the exposure time was progressively reduced to systematically decrease the signal-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 309.29pt, "to-noise ratio. In these measurements, we used a tunable laser and an Allied Vision camera. The exposure ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 321.89pt, "time was stepwise decreased starting from the longest acquisition (1800 ms) - initially in 200 ms ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 334.61pt, "intervals down to 200 ms, and subsequently in finer 50 ms increments down to 100 ms. This approach ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 347.33pt, "enabled us to evaluate how noise evolves as the detected signal becomes progressively weaker. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 367.85pt, "Figure S1 shows, with blue points, how the number of distinct gray levels in the hologram histograms ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 380.57pt, "decreases with shorter exposure times. Noise levels were quantified via STD within a background region ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 393.19pt, "of the USAF target devoid of structural features, and the corresponding standard deviations are plotted ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 405.91pt, "for both reconstruction methods (AS and PSR with TV). Single-frame AS results are marked with “×”, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 418.51pt, "whereas PSR with TV results are marked with “*”. For exposure times below 100 ms, the recorded ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 431.11pt, "signal collapsed into only two gray levels, becoming dominated by noise and unsuitable for meaningful ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 443.95pt, "reconstruction. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 464.47pt, "A noteworthy observation is that the noise level remained relatively stable down to an exposure time of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 477.07pt, "approximately 600 ms, which corresponds to histograms containing several gray levels (~10). Within ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 489.79pt, "this range, both reconstruction approaches exhibited stable, method-specific noise levels - AS retaining ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.39pt, "its characteristic noise and PSR with TV maintaining substantially lower noise - despite the strongly ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 514.99pt, "reduced optical power reaching the detector. This underscores the potential of LH-DUV to image ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.71pt, "biological samples under low-illumination conditions without introducing significant photodamage, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 540.31pt, "while still maintaining reconstruction quality comparable to data acquired under standard illumination ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.18pt, "(both in terms of resolution and signal-to-noise ratio). ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 573.7pt, "When the signal was further reduced by shortening the exposure time below this threshold, the noise ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 586.3pt, "increased exponentially. Nevertheless, PSR with TV continued to provide substantial noise suppression ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 599.02pt, "even under extremely low-photon-budget conditions. It should be emphasized, however, that in the most ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 611.62pt, "extreme cases - such as holograms containing only three gray levels and similar borderline conditions - ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 624.34pt, "the achievable reconstruction resolution becomes limited by the noise floor itself. ")
]

